<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Reditus in talks on stake.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Reditus in talks on stake.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer and information technology group Reditus-SGPS said it had begun talks with investment fund Greenville Securities Ltd, which wants a stake in the Portuguese concern.</p>
<p>Sources close to the talks said that Greenville Securities wanted a stake of between 10 and 20 percent.</p>
<p>A statement issued by Reditus said merely that preliminary discussions had started.</p>
<p>Reditus closed at 595 escudos on Monday, down 17 on its previous close.</p>
<p>(( --Lisbon bureau 3511-3113125))</p>
</text>
